<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sacro Regio Consiglio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1442">1442</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Sacred Royal Council</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sacro Regio Consiglio was the supreme court of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, created by Alfonso V of Aragon after his conquest of the kingdom in 1442. Presided over by a senior jurist, it heard appeals from the kingdom's other courts and became the centre of Neapolitan legal culture, whose decisions were widely collected and cited. It remained the highest tribunal until the French reforms of the early nineteenth century.</p></div>
